(Colette Kress -- Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Thanks, Simona. Q4 revenue was $3.11 billion, up 41% year-on-year and up 3% sequentially, well) Tj
T*
( above our outlook, reflecting upside in our data center and gaming businesses. Full year ) Tj
T*
(revenue was $10.9 billion, down 7%, we recovered from the excess channel inventory in gaming ) Tj
T*
(and an earlier pause in hyperscale spending, and exited the year with great momentum. Starting) Tj
T*
( with gaming, revenue of $1.49 billion was up 56% year-on-year and down 10% sequentially. Full) Tj
T*
( year gaming revenue was $5.52 billion, down 12% from our prior year. We enjoyed strong end-) Tj
T*
(demand for our desktop and notebook GPUs. Let me give you some more details.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Our gaming lineup was exceptionally well positioned for the holidays with unique ray tracing ) Tj
T*
(capabilities of our RTX GPUs, an incredible performance at every price point. From the Singles) Tj
T*
( Day shopping event in China through the Christmas season in the West, channel demand was ) Tj
T*
(strong for our entire stack. Fueling this were new blockbuster games like Call of Duty: Modern) Tj
T*
( Warfare, continued eSports momentum, and new RTX Super products with RTX price points as low ) Tj
T*
(as $299, ray tracing is now the sweet spot for PC gamers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Gaming is thriving, and gamers prefer GeForce. The global phenomenon of eSports keeps gaming ) Tj
T*
(momentum with an audience now exceeding $440 million, up over 30% in just two years, according) Tj
T*
( to Newzoo. The League of Legends World Championship brought more than a 100 million viewers ) Tj
T*
(on par with this month's Super Bowl. Ray tracing titles continue to come to market and GeForce) Tj
T*
( RTX GPUs are the only ones that support this important technology. This quarter Wolfenstein: ) Tj
T*
(Youngblood and Deliver Us The Moon were the latest titles to support ray tracing, as well as ) Tj
T*
(NVIDIA's deep learning, super sampling technique, which also uses AI to boost performance. ) Tj
T*
(With the proliferation of RTX-enabled games and our best ever top to bottom performance, we ) Tj
T*
(are solidly into the Turing architecture upgrade cycle. Gamers continue to move to higher-end ) Tj
T*
(GPUs to gain better performance and support for ray tracing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Gaming laptops posted double-digit year-on-year growth for the eighth consecutive quarter. The) Tj
T*
( category continues to expand, driving by appealing, thin and light form factors with ) Tj
T*
(fantastic graphics performance. This holiday season retailers stocked a record 125 gaming ) Tj
T*
(laptops based on NVIDIA GPUs, up from 94 last year with our Max-Q designs up two times. At ) Tj
T*
(CES, we launched the world's first 14-inch GeForce RTX laptop with Asus. We also continue to ) Tj
T*
(expand our Studio line-up of laptops for the fast growing population, our freelance creators, ) Tj
T*
(designers and YouTubers, with 13 new RTX Studio systems introduced at CES. Powered by Turing ) Tj
T*
(GPUs, these systems are optimized for over 55 creative and design applications with RTX ) Tj
T*
(accelerated ray tracing and/or AI.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Last week, we launched our GeForce NOW cloud gaming service powered by GeForce. GeForce NOW is) Tj
T*
( the first cloud gaming service to deliver ray-traced games. It's also the only open platform,) Tj
T*
( so gamers can enjoy the games they already have and use their existing store accounts without) Tj
T*
( having to repurchase games. GeForce NOW enables PC games on Macs, Windows, PCs, TVs, mobile ) Tj
T*
(devices and soon Chromebooks. GFN has a freemium business model that includes two membership ) Tj
T*
(plans. A free membership with standard access and a founders tier with a starting price of ) Tj
T*
($4.99 per month, which gives priority access and RTX ray tracing support.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Our goal with GeForce NOW is to expand GeForce gaming to more gamers. About 80% of GeForce NOW) Tj
T*
( gamers are playing on underpowered PCs or devices with Mac OS or Android. With GeForce NOW, ) Tj
T*
(they are able to enjoy PC gaming on a GeForce GPU in the cloud. GeForce NOW can expand GeForce) Tj
T*
( well beyond to roughly 200 million gamers we reach today. Separately, we entered into a ) Tj
T*
(collaboration with Tencent, the world's largest gaming platform to bring PC gaming in the ) Tj
T*
(cloud to China, the world's largest gaming market. NVIDIA GPU Technology will power Tencent's ) Tj
T*
(START cloud gaming service, which is in early testing stages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Moving to data center. Revenue was a record $968 million, up 43% year-on-year and up 33% ) Tj
T*
(sequentially. Our strongest ever sequential growth in dollar terms. Full-year fiscal year '20 ) Tj
T*
(datacenter revenue was a record $2.98 billion, up 2% from the prior year. Strong growth was ) Tj
T*
(fueled by hyperscale, and vertical industry and customers. Hyperscale demand was driven by ) Tj
